From 126c969c93bec712a34feee5a5b7259305c45b65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sfxnz <sfxnz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:33:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] inkling2: fuse keyed DFlash2 selector, fix graph key, and
 wire calibrated CHANCES + Landing

Implement Lever 4 and Lever 8c (100% lossless) for Inkling-2-Mini DFlash2:

- dflash2.cuh / dflash2_cuda.zig:
  - Fuse multi-step candidate selection + bit-exact keyed Gumbel race
    (race_u matching sample.cu bit-for-bit, toggled via TF_INKLING2_DRAFT_KEYED=1)
    + per-step softmax probability output into a single tf_ink2_df_select[8]_batch
    launch per round (replacing up to 7 + 7*count serial launches).
  - Fix the latent b.ns graph-key bug by collapsing DFlash2 proposal graph Key
    to { k, sum_n } (slot- and rule-independent).
  - Remove redundant cuMemcpyDtoDAsync(a.mixed, a.matrix) in absorb / absorbBatch
    by writing addNorm directly into a.normed.
  - Coalesce staging HtoD uploads (AbsorbStage, ProposeStage) and walk+chances
    DtoH download (ProposeOut) into 1 DMA each.

- dspark_cuda.zig / loop_backend.zig / loop_drafter.zig:
  - Store held_chances and anchor on Session (host-only, zero GPU VRAM change).
  - Wire Backend.vtable.probabilities + lanes.draft_tree.Landing online
    calibration (separate greedy and sampled tables) behind
    TF_INKLING2_DFLASH2_CHANCES=1 (lone streams by default; optional
    TF_INKLING2_DFLASH2_CHANCES_SHARED=1 and TF_INKLING2_DRAFT_CONFIDENCE).
  - Export draft_probabilities, granted_depth, and draft_slack=7 in facts() so
    c1 adapts verify width dynamically (1-2 rows on uncertain tokens, 5-7 rows
    on confident spans) while c4 retains shared_guard uniform depth control.

Credits (for NOTICE, Apache-2.0 / MIT):
- Fused keyed DraftKey selector, softmax chances, and Landing calibration
  adapted from MiaAI-Lab (commit 9e3cf20b, patch 0018-mini-dflash2-drafter.patch)
  and tonyd2wild (commit 2fe0eb57, patch 0018).
